{
  "declined": "none",
  "items": [
    {
      "i": 0,
      "revised": "Since the pandemic, working from home has become widespread.",
      "why": "把 \"has become common since the pandemic\" 改為更精準流暢的字詞 \"has become widespread\" 並把時間狀語放前面，使句子更自然。",
      "zh": "自從疫情以來，在家工作已經變得普遍。"
    },
    {
      "i": 1,
      "revised": "For one thing, employees reclaim the hours formerly lost to commuting, which they can instead devote to their families.",
      "why": "將 \"save the time of commuting\" 變為更精確的表達 \"reclaim the hours formerly lost to commuting\" 並用 \"devote to\" 替代 \"spend with\" 以提高語言層次。",
      "zh": "一方面，員工奪回了過去花在通勤上的時間，這些時間可以改用來陪伴家人。"
    },
    {
      "i": 2,
      "revised": "Conversely, many people experience loneliness because they lack face-to-face interaction.",
      "why": "把 \"On the other hand\" 換成更正式的連接詞 \"Conversely\"，修正語法錯誤 \"lack of\" 為正確用法 \"lack\" 並用 \"interaction\" 替代重複的 \"communication\" 以增進表達精確度。",
      "zh": "相反地，許多人感到孤單，因為他們缺乏面對面的互動。"
    },
    {
      "i": 3,
      "revised": "I contend that a hybrid model, in which staff attend the office two days per week, offers the most balanced solution.",
      "why": "將 \"In my opinion\" 換為更成熟的 \"I contend that\"，並把 \"where staff come to the office\" 改為更正式的 \"in which staff attend the office\" 以提升語體與流暢度。",
      "zh": "我主張採用混合模式，員工每週到辦公室兩天，這是最平衡的解決方案。"
    }
  ]
}
